# Scaling Workflow for High-Velocity Hiring

A systems-driven workflow for scaling teams rapidly without sacrificing signal quality, velocity, or decision integrity.

---

## 1. Intake and Role Architecture

Objective: Define what "good" looks like before the loop begins.

- Structured intake with hiring manager
- Clarify business need, success outcomes, and capability requirements
- Translate ambiguous requirements into calibrated success profiles
- Define competencies, must-haves, nice-to-haves, and dealbreakers
- Align on velocity expectations and decision timelines
- Document intake in a shared brief

---

## 2. Interview Loop Design

Objective: Build a loop that produces high signal without slowing velocity.

- Determine required stages (no redundancy)
- Select high-signal interviewers only
- Assign competencies to each interviewer
- Build structured rubrics and scorecards
- Define pass/fail criteria
- Create interviewer instructions
- Build shared spreadsheet or dashboard for visibility

---

## 3. Sourcing and Pipeline Build

Objective: Build a high-signal pipeline aligned to the calibrated success profile.

- Boolean search and passive sourcing
- AI-enhanced sourcing workflows
- GitHub, Dice, and market intelligence for technical-adjacent roles
- Personalized outreach sequences
- DEI-centered sourcing logic
- Shared spreadsheet tracking pipeline stages

---

## 4. Stage 1: Screening

Objective: Filter out noise before candidates enter the loop.

- Validate capability and alignment
- Identify gaps early
- Set expectations
- Document signal
- Prevent misaligned candidates from entering the loop

---

## 5. Stage 2: Hiring Manager Meet and Greet

Objective: Prevent late-stage churn through early alignment.

- Introduce role context
- Validate communication style
- Confirm business fit
- Ensure candidate understands expectations
- Capture hiring manager feedback

---

## 6. Stage 3: Technical or Functional Evaluation

Objective: Measure real capability using structured evaluation.

- Interviewers evaluate assigned competencies only
- Use structured rubrics
- Scorecards capture signal consistently
- Remove bias and noise
- Document signal

---

## 7. Stage 4: Wrap-Up and Final Alignment

Objective: Make fast, high-quality decisions without drift.

- Align feedback
- Resolve conflicting signals
- Validate compensation alignment
- Confirm motivation
- Move to offer quickly

---

## 8. Offer Strategy and Close

Objective: Convert high-value candidates in competitive markets.

- Tailored offer strategy
- Compensation alignment
- Clear communication
- Fast turnaround
- Document acceptance

---

## 9. Post-Hire Feedback Loop

Objective: Strengthen the system with every hire.

- Review pass-through rates
- Identify bottlenecks
- Adjust loop architecture
- Recalibrate success profiles
- Update scorecards
- Improve interviewer alignment

---

